  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fill the interior of each non\u2011zero colored region with the color 8.\n    A cell is considered interior if all four orthogonal neighbours\n    (up, down, left, right) exist and have the same original colour.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Deep copy of the input grid for the result\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Orthogonal neighbours\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            col = grid[i][j]\n            if col == 0:\n                continue\n\n            interior = True\n            for di, dj in dirs:\n                ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                # If any neighbour is outside or different, this cell is on the border\n                if not (0 <= ni < rows and 0 <= nj < cols) or grid[ni][nj] != col:\n                    interior = False\n                    break\n\n            if interior:\n                out[i][j] = 8\n\n    return out",
